      "reasons": [
        "The definition’s core characterization—\"degree to which another person is personally connected or meaningful to someone\"—is not explicitly stated in the provided packet. The packet describes \"self-relevance\" in terms of recipients differing in extents (friends vs. acquaintances vs. strangers) but does not define it as personal connectedness/meaningfulness.",
        "The definition goes beyond the packet by presenting a general, conceptual definition of the term rather than sticking to what the packet supports (i.e., self-relevance operationalized via social distance categories and its association with selective generosity).",
        "The second sentence about higher self-relevance being linked to more generous sharing is supported by the packet, but the first sentence is not."
